{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790275497,"nonce":"mpEJNkEaUJISJU13PDdLlRjR8Qw=","title":"Python: a loop threading a tuple through a tuple-returning call segfaults intermittently at Cranelift after OSR","message":"Reproducer (Mac arm64, main 8844ca79, release zypy built without or with the LLVM tier; the LLVM tier is not involved):\n\n    def step(t: tuple[int, int, int], k: int) -\u003e tuple[int, int, int]:\n        a, b, c = t\n        return (b + k, c, (a * 7 + k) % 1000003)\n\n    def run(n: int) -\u003e int:\n        t = (1, 2, 3)\n        total = 0\n        for i in range(n):\n            t = step(t, i)\n            total = (total + t[0] + t[2]) % 1000000007\n        return total\n\n    print(run(20000))\n\n`zypy run t.py` exits 139 (SIGSEGV) in roughly 2 of 16 runs, with nothing printed. With ZYNTAX_DISABLE_OSR=1, 16 of 16 runs pass, so the crash follows the interpreted frame leaving through the outlined resume point of run's loop. With ZYPY_LLVM=1 ZYNTAX_DISABLE_INTERP_OPTS=1 and a one-second wait between two calls of run the rate is 3 to 4 in 16; the trace of a crashing debug run ends at\n\n    [osr] run site=0x...: outlined resume point\n    [osr] interpreted frame leaves at site=0x... -\u003e 0x...\n\nbefore step is compiled at all. Under lldb it did not reproduce in 12 runs (timing-dependent). CPython prints 164768848 for run(20000) twice when called as in crates/zyntax_python/tests/fixtures/llvm_tuple_entry.py.\n\nSuspect: the tuple live-in `t` (a multi-field struct held by reference) handed from the interpreter to the outlined region, e.g. its storage not outliving the interpreter frame, or the region's first call of step reaching a lazy stub with the tuple's address.","files":null}]}